# Line endings are part of the content here.
#
# manifest.json records the sha256 of every file, and the plugin checks its
# vendored copy against those hashes. Git's autocrlf would hand a Windows
# checkout CRLF versions of files whose hashes were taken over LF, so every
# document would read as corrupt on one platform and fine on another — for a
# reason that has nothing to do with what the documents say.
#
# So: LF everywhere, on every platform, whatever the local setting.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
